cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the project report it accompanies."
title: "AI-Based Energy-Optimal Train Speed Profile Generation Using Neural Surrogate Modeling for Real-Time Railway Systems"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Karcha"
    given-names: "Mohamed Amine"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/thelordofpigeons/train-speed-profile-surrogate"
date-released: 2026-10-05
abstract: >-
  A PyTorch neural surrogate that predicts energy-optimal train speed
  profiles in milliseconds instead of the seconds to minutes needed by
  optimal control solvers. The network uses positional encoding, modulated
  residual blocks, track-feature conditioning, hard boundary-condition
  enforcement and physics-informed losses. The training dataset is
  confidential and is not included.
keywords:
  - railway
  - energy-optimal train control
  - neural surrogate
  - physics-informed learning
  - speed profile
